Title: Sixty-Six Million
Credit: Written by
Author: Previz Stage
Draft date: 2026-10-25

EXT. CRETACEOUS RIVER VALLEY - DUSK

A wide prehistoric valley under a bruised orange sky. Giant ferns and cycads crowd the near bank of a slow brown river. Towering conifers and a smoking volcano stand on the far side. Dragonflies the size of hawks drift through the haze.

DR. NOOR HADDAD (40s, wiry, grey-streaked black hair under a battered field hat, a khaki expedition jacket over a sweat-dark shirt, hiking boots) crouches behind a mossy boulder, a bulky brass chronometer strapped to her wrist.

KAI (20s, tall, lanky, close-cropped hair, a torn orange survival vest over a grey thermal, cargo trousers) drops beside her, out of breath.

A huge Tyrannosaurus rex lumbers slowly across the clearing right in front of them, close enough to feel each step, its tail sweeping the ferns, head low, scenting the air.

KAI
(whispering)
Tell me the window reopens in under a minute.

NOOR
Fourteen minutes.

KAI
Fourteen.

NOOR
(eyes on the animal)
Don't move. It can't see what doesn't move.

The T. rex pauses, turns its head toward the boulder, then walks on toward the river.

KAI
That's a myth. Everyone knows that's a myth.

NOOR
Then don't test it.
